SUMMARY:Global Health Colloquium: Drug Policy and the Future of Global He
 alth Advocacy
DESCRIPTION:rawing on more than three decades of work at the intersection
  of drug policy\, HIV\, public health\, and human rights\, Dr Kasia Mali
 nowska-Sempruch of the Open Society Foundation will explore why drug pol
 icy should be understood as a central global health issue. The talk will
  examine the connections between drug policy\, infectious disease\, over
 dose\, criminalization\, and organized crime\, while reflecting on lesso
 ns from her career advancing drug policy reform around the world. It wil
 l also consider the distinctive role that philanthropic and civil societ
 y organizations such as Open Society play wi\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/
 events/2026/global-health-colloquium-drug-policy-and-future-global-healt
 h-advocacy
